 "title": "Negative Numbers",
 "summary": "Learn how signs work so you can add, subtract, multiply, divide and solve real-life temperature questions below zero.",
 "blocks": [
  {
   "kind": "paragraph",
   "text": "# Adding and Subtracting Negative Numbers"
  },
  {
   "kind": "paragraph",
   "text": "To add and subtract negative numbers we can use a number line.  \nWhen we add we move to the right and when we subtract we move to the left."
  },
  {
   "kind": "figure",
   "figure_ref": "assets/001-negativenumbers1.jpg",
   "alt": "negativenumbers1"
  },
  {
   "kind": "worked-example",
   "title": "Example 1: \\-3 + 5",
   "steps": [
    {
     "heading": null,
     "body": "The first number is the starting point. We start at -3.  \nWe are adding so we are moving to the right.  \nWe move 5 spaces to the right.  \n**\\-3 + 5 = 2**",
     "figure_refs": []
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "kind": "worked-example",
   "title": "Example 2: \\-2 - 6",
   "steps": [
    {
     "heading": null,
     "body": "The first number is the starting point. We start at -2.  \nWe are subtracting so we are moving to the left.  \nWe move 6 spaces to the left.  \n**\\-2 - 6 = -8**",
     "figure_refs": []
    }
   ]
  },
  {
