  {
   "kind": "paragraph",
   "text": "# Multiplying and Dividing Negative Numbers"
  },
  {
   "kind": "paragraph",
   "text": "When we multiply negative numbers we use the rules:**  \nPositive × Positive = Positive  \nPositive × Negative = Negative  \nNegative × Positive = Negative  \nNegative × Negative = Positive**"
  },
  {
   "kind": "paragraph",
   "text": "The rules for multiplying and dividing negative numbers are the same:**  \nPositive ÷ Positive = Positive  \nPositive ÷ Negative = Negative  \nNegative ÷ Positive = Negative  \nNegative ÷ Negative = Positive**"
  },
  {
   "kind": "worked-example",
   "title": "Example 5: \\-6 × 2",
   "steps": [
    {
     "heading": null,
     "body": "6 × 2 = 12  \nNegative × Positive = Negative  \n**\\-6 × 2 = -12**",
     "figure_refs": []
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "kind": "worked-example",
   "title": "Example 6: 7 × -5",
   "steps": [
    {
     "heading": null,
     "body": "7 × 5 = 35  \nPositive × Negative = Negative  \n**7 × -5 = -35**",
     "figure_refs": []
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "kind": "worked-example",
   "title": "Example 7: \\-9 × -4",
   "steps": [
    {
     "heading": null,
     "body": "9 × 4 = 36  \nNegative × Negative = Positive.  \n**\\-9 × -4 = 36**",
     "figure_refs": []
    }
   ]
  },
